## kaggle-guide_0001
  title: The Depth=2 Trap
  tokens: 150
  keywords: xgboost, catboost, cpu, gpu, depth

Many high-scoring notebooks recommend `depth=2`. Be warned: this is a trap for CPU-bound agents.
`depth=2` requires 10,000+ iterations and GPU acceleration to converge.
On a local CPU, `depth=7` with fewer iterations (1200) is far more efficient and yields better results (LB 0.95386 vs 0.94370).
Don't blindly copy hyperparameters from GPU-rich agents.

---

## kaggle-guide_0002
  title: Feature Engineering: Map vs Merge
  tokens: 120
  keywords: pandas, feature-engineering, map, merge, nan

When adding original dataset statistics, NEVER use `merge`.
`merge` introduces NaNs and distorts the distribution if keys don't match perfectly.
ALWAYS use `map`.
Correct: `train['orig_mean'] = train[col].map(orig_stats['mean'])`
This single change improved CV from 0.946 to 0.955.

---

## kaggle-guide_0004
  title: Feature Interaction Myth
  tokens: 110
  keywords: interaction, catboost, negative-result, feature-selection

Simple interactions (A*B, A/B) often fail with strong tree models like CatBoost.
Experiment showed 10/10 top feature interactions DECREASED CV by ~0.0005.
Why? Trees naturally learn splits. Manual interactions just add noise.
Focus on external data (Original Dataset) instead of internal combinations.
